    controversy_html: `<p>The primary criticism is cosmetic inflation—operator skins ($20-25) are pricier than competitors' offerings. Additionally, the base game purchase ($69.99) plus cosmetics creates a higher total cost of ownership compared to free-to-play Warzone. Some players feel cosmetics appear in limited-time bundles to create artificial scarcity, exploiting FOMO psychology.</p>`,
